## Original Content
Archeologists are confronting an “unfathomable” loss as border wall construction is set to cut across ranches that are home to unique historical sites, many of which haven’t been fully studied.

## Summary
Border wall construction is threatening archaeological sites with up to 6,000 years of history on private ranches. Archaeologists are concerned about the significant loss of these understudied historical resources due to the construction cutting across these lands.

## Key Points
- Border wall construction is impacting private ranches that contain unique historical sites.
- Many of these sites have up to 6,000 years of history and have not been fully studied.
- Archaeologists fear an 'unfathomable' loss of cultural heritage as construction proceeds.
- The construction is set to directly cut across these lands, risking irreversible damage to historical artifacts.


